    "done_when": "the scope check in reckon/crew/promotion.py (near line 3950, _cumulative_diff(base=commit_list[0]^, head=commit_list[-1])) counts only paths changed by the cited commits that are not reachable from the integration branch, excluding merge commits (for example git log --no-merges main..head over the cited set, or per-commit diffs of the cited non-merge commits), so a run whose last commit sits on a merge from main is charged with its own paths only; a run with a genuinely out-of-scope path in its own commit is still refused; tests/test_promotion_scope_counts_only_the_runs_commits.py builds a synthesised temporary repository where a run commits inside its fence, main advances with a peer commit touching another path, the run merges main and commits again, and asserts promotion counts only the run paths, plus a sibling case where the run itself touches an out-of-scope path and is still refused; the real config home is untouched; restoring the first^..last tree diff turns the merge case red; the promotion test files show zero added failures against the dispatch base with base and head failure ids recorded",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "make promotion measure a run write scope from the paths its own cited commits change rather than a tree diff that spans main history merged into the run head",
